iRIEL-AI CORE AI
STATUS: CANONICAL INSTITUTIONAL CONTRACT
iRiel-AI Core AI is the intelligence capability contract of iRiel Personal Intelligence within the PRSL-AI Ecosystem.
Core AI provides the computational intelligence capabilities that iRiel Personal Intelligence may use to understand, reason, generate, transform, interpret, plan, analyze, and assist.
Core AI is a capability layer.
It is not the identity of iRiel.
It is not the Principle.
It is not iRiel Personal Intelligence itself.
It is not iRiel Maestro Resonance.
It is not iRiel Router Intelligence.
It is not iRiel Intelligence Server.
It is not iRiel System.
It is not iRiel-AI Device’s.
Core AI exists to provide intelligence capabilities to the Personal Intelligence environment under the contracts that govern the ecosystem.
The foundational Principle remains:
Accessibility and Inclusion with Privacy by Default.
Core AI must therefore operate in service of that Principle.
INTELLIGENCE WITHOUT IDENTITY
Core AI may provide intelligence.
It does not become iRiel.
A model may reason.
A provider may generate.
A service may process.
A local runtime may infer.
None of these capabilities independently constitute the identity of iRiel Personal Intelligence.
The relationship is:
Human
↓
iRiel Personal Intelligence
↓
iRiel Maestro Resonance
↓
iRiel Router Intelligence
↓
iRiel-AI Core AI
↓
Intelligence Capability
Core AI is therefore subordinate to the Personal Intelligence architecture.
The intelligence provider is replaceable.
The intelligence capability is replaceable.
The implementation is replaceable.
The identity and constitutional principles remain.
AI-AGNOSTIC INTELLIGENCE
Core AI must remain AI-agnostic.
The architecture may integrate:
On-device models
Apple Intelligence
OpenAI
Gemini
Anthropic
Other commercial providers
Open-source models
Specialized models
Deterministic intelligence systems
Future AI systems
Other authorized intelligence providers
No provider is constitutionally privileged merely because it currently supplies intelligence.
A provider may be preferred for a particular capability.
That preference is operational.
It is not identity.
A provider may be removed without destroying iRiel Personal Intelligence.
A model may be replaced without destroying iRiel Personal Intelligence.
An AI architecture may evolve without destroying iRiel Personal Intelligence.
Core AI must therefore provide a stable architectural capability boundary above replaceable intelligence implementations.
