Protected according to applicable privacy requirements
Core AI must not assume that all available Personal Intelligence context should be passed into every intelligence operation.
More context does not automatically mean better intelligence.
The correct context is the context necessary to serve the human appropriately.
MEMORY
Core AI does not own iRiel Memory.
Memory belongs to the Personal Intelligence architecture.
Core AI may use authorized memory as input when the broader architecture determines that it is relevant and permitted.
Core AI must not independently convert every interaction into permanent memory.
It must not bypass memory policy.
It must not treat generated content as automatically authoritative memory.
Memory remains governed separately.
